WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:18.754
My name is Mary Chilton. I am one of the original Pilgrims to set sail for the New World in a ship called the Mayflower.

2
00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:22.969
A Pilgrim is a person who makes a journey for a religious reason.

3
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.201
The story of the Pilgrims begins in Holland.

4
00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:32.344
Even though I am English, I was born in Leyden, Holland, in 1607.

5
00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:39.787
My family lived in Holland because we were not free to practice our religion in England, but Holland wasn't our home.

6
00:00:39.788 --> 00:00:42.333
It was a strange and foreign land.

7
00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:46.165
I lived there with my parents for 12 years.

8
00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:51.771
In 1619 we returned to England to prepare for a voyage to the New World.

9
00:00:51.772 --> 00:00:59.295
My parents and many other adults packed trunks and barrels with all the things we would need to begin life in the New World.

10
00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:06.561
They hired two ships, the Mayflower and the Speedwell, to take us to the New World.

11
00:01:06.562 --> 00:01:10.548
We were all very excited and a little scared.

12
00:01:10.549 --> 00:01:18.532
We left England on August 5, 1620, but we had to return to England because the Speedwell was leaking.

13
00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:22.889
We tried to fix the ship, but it was too old and tired.

14
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:32.484
We were forced to abandon it, leaving behind our cooking oil and some other valuables. We all piled into the Mayflower.

15
00:01:32.485 --> 00:01:37.853
We finally set sail for the New World on September 6, 1620.

16
00:01:37.854 --> 00:01:41.781
There were 130 people aboard the Mayflower.

17
00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:51.395
There were 102 Pilgrims and about 28 crew members. Three of the women were pregnant!

18
00:01:51.396 --> 00:01:55.505
It took us 66 days to reach the New World.

19
00:01:55.506 --> 00:02:02.144
Many of us became seasick when the Mayflower was tossed around by storms and strong waves.

20
00:02:02.145 --> 00:02:09.575
I spent many days being sick below deck because going above deck was dangerous.

21
00:02:09.576 --> 00:02:15.743
The wind, rain, and waves made the deck slippery, so it was easy to fall overboard.

22
00:02:15.744 --> 00:02:20.366
When it wasn't stormy and scary, the voyage was boring.

23
00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:28.342
At home I was never bored because I was busy helping my mother with the sewing, the laundry, or the cooking.

24
00:02:28.343 --> 00:02:33.828
But, on the Mayflower, there was very little women's work that needed to be done.

25
00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:39.050
I could have died, not from seasickness, but from boredom.

26
00:02:39.051 --> 00:02:44.081
Luckily, I had two friends, Constance Hopkins and Elizabeth Tilley.

27
00:02:44.082 --> 00:02:49.032
They made me laugh with their stories.

28
00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:53.877
Elizabeth was in love with John Howland, but he took no notice of her.

29
00:02:53.878 --> 00:02:59.417
It was both funny and sad, but never boring to watch her unrequited love.

30
00:02:59.418 --> 00:03:05.207
When we weren't listening to Elizabeth, we were often trying to avoid Francis Billington.

31
00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:11.744
He was a bully who liked to pull our hair. He was such a troublemaker!

32
00:03:11.745 --> 00:03:17.591
Once, he started a fire on board the Mayflower when he shot his father's gun below deck.

33
00:03:17.592 --> 00:03:22.063
Luckily, everyone heard the sound and put the fire out.

34
00:03:22.064 --> 00:03:30.577
The scariest moment aboard the Mayflower was when the ship was caught in a terrible storm for two whole days.

35
00:03:30.578 --> 00:03:37.698
In the single room below deck where we all lived, we huddled together and prayed to God to save us.

36
00:03:37.699 --> 00:03:47.641
We weren't sure that God was listening, however, because on the second day of the storm, one of the main beams below deck cracked.

37
00:03:47.642 --> 00:03:54.591
Many of the sailors were scared because they knew that the ship couldn't survive another storm.

38
00:03:54.592 --> 00:04:00.387
The passengers also feared they would die. But God was merciful.

39
00:04:00.388 --> 00:04:06.155
No other storms caught us, and only two men died on the voyage.

40
00:04:06.156 --> 00:04:11.030
On November 9, 1620, we finally saw land.

41
00:04:11.031 --> 00:04:17.371
The ship's captain called the place Cape Cod, and he said it was many miles north of Virginia.

42
00:04:17.372 --> 00:04:25.585
We were all glad to see land after having spent 66 days in a small room with 102 seasick people.

43
00:04:25.586 --> 00:04:33.045
We were also looking forward to breathing fresh air because the Mayflower smelled most unpleasant!

44
00:04:33.046 --> 00:04:41.259
On November 13, 1620, I was the first woman to step off of the Mayflower into the New World.

45
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.246
I went ashore to help with the laundry.

46
00:04:44.247 --> 00:04:55.052
It was the only time in my life I was ever thankful to God for making laundry women's work, because it allowed me to stand firmly on the ground.

47
00:04:55.053 --> 00:05:04.135
We wanted to continue south to Virginia because there were other Englishmen who had settled there, but our attempt to sail south failed.

48
00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:09.294
The ship didn't dare go far from shore because of the damage to the beam.

49
00:05:09.295 --> 00:05:13.079
So we decided to remain in Cape Cod.

50
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:19.540
We sent the men out to explore, and on December 12, 1620, the men returned.

51
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:25.802
They had found a suitable place. They had also made contact with Native Americans.

52
00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:33.026
On December 15, 1620, we went ashore and started our new life in the New World.

53
00:05:33.027 --> 00:05:43.913
It wouldn't be an easy life, but we were hopeful.
